---
system: sys-16-parent-mobile-application
flow_id: token-refresh-mobile
surface: mobile
spec_anchor: /software/systems/16-parent-mobile-application#5-7-api-client-with-token-refresh
actors: [ParentApp, Gateway, IdentityService]
apis:
  - POST /v1/auth/refresh
externals: [ExpoSecureStore]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - invalid_refresh_token
  - refresh_inflight_collision
  - auth_refresh_rate_limited
  - secure_store_unavailable
idempotency: in-app refresh-inflight flag + subscriber queue serializes concurrent 401s — only one POST /v1/auth/refresh is in flight at a time
retry: queued 401-bearing requests retry once after refresh succeeds — on refresh failure, clear tokens and emit AUTH_FAILURE (no further retry)
timeout: refresh call 15s axios default — queued original requests inherit caller timeout
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED. Mobile-side companion to 01-identity/token-refresh — captures the in-app singleton-refresh contract (isRefreshing flag + refreshSubscribers queue) per spec §5.7.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant IdentityService

    ParentApp->>Gateway: any /v1/* request and Bearer (expired) access token
    Gateway->>Gateway: JWT verify — token expired
    Gateway-->>ParentApp: 401 SESSION_EXPIRED
    Note over ParentApp: response interceptor traps 401 — check isRefreshing flag
    alt refresh already in flight
        Note over ParentApp: queue this request — push callback into refreshSubscribers
    else first 401
        ParentApp->>ParentApp: set isRefreshing = true
        ParentApp->>ParentApp: read refreshToken from expo-secure-store
        alt secure_store_unavailable
            ParentApp-->>ParentApp: clearTokens and emit AUTH_FAILURE
        else stored token present
            ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/auth/refresh {refreshToken}
            Gateway->>IdentityService: forward
            alt auth_refresh_rate_limited
                Gateway-->>ParentApp: 429 — clearTokens and emit AUTH_FAILURE
            else invalid_refresh_token
                IdentityService-->>Gateway: 401 invalid_refresh_token
                Gateway-->>ParentApp: 401 — clearTokens and emit AUTH_FAILURE
            else success
                IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {tokens: {accessToken, refreshToken}}
                Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
                ParentApp->>ParentApp: storeTokens and isRefreshing = false
                Note over ParentApp: flush refreshSubscribers — each callback retries its original request with new Bearer
            end
        end
    end

    Note over ParentApp,IdentityService: refresh-inflight singleton prevents N concurrent /v1/auth/refresh calls when N requests hit 401 simultaneously — see spec §5.7
